BT /F2 17 Tf 54 730.0 Td (Identity & Authentication Policy) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 703.0 Td (Hewlett Packard Enterprise \(HPE\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 689.0 Td (Document ID: HPE-SEC-D5 | Version 3.2 | Effective Date: 2026-07-08) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 675.0 Td (Owner: Office of the Chief Information Security Officer \(CISO\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 661.0 Td (Classification: Internal Use) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 641.0 Td (---) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 615.0 Td (1. Purpose and Scope) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 592.0 Td (This Identity & Authentication Policy establishes the mandatory requirements governing how digital) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 578.0 Td (identities are provisioned, verified, and retired across Hewlett Packard Enterprise. It applies to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 564.0 Td (all employees, contractors, service accounts, and third-party partners who access HPE systems,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 550.0 Td (applications, and data-whether hosted on-premises, in HPE GreenLake, or in third-party cloud) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 536.0 Td (environments. Adherence to this policy is required to protect corporate assets, customer data, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 522.0 Td (HPE's global operations from unauthorized access and credential-based attack.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 496.0 Td (2. Identity Federation and Single Sign-On) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 473.0 Td (HPE standardizes on a federated identity model built on Okta as the primary Single Sign-On \(SSO\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 459.0 Td (broker, integrated with Microsoft Entra ID as an authoritative identity provider for Microsoft 365) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 445.0 Td (and Azure-based workloads. All new applications MUST integrate with the corporate SSO platform using) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 431.0 Td (modern federation protocols-SAML 2.0 or OpenID Connect \(OIDC\)-in preference to local authentication) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 417.0 Td (stores. Federation reduces password sprawl, centralizes access enforcement, and ensures that) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 403.0 Td (de-provisioning is immediate and comprehensive. Legacy applications that cannot support SAML or OIDC) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 389.0 Td (must be documented as exceptions, remediated on a defined roadmap, and protected by compensating) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 375.0 Td (controls. Direct LDAP or basic authentication to production systems is prohibited unless explicitly) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 361.0 Td (approved by the Identity Governance team.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 335.0 Td (3. Multi-Factor Authentication) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 312.0 Td (Multi-factor authentication \(MFA\) is mandatory for all interactive access to HPE resources;) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 298.0 Td (single-factor sign-in is never sufficient for corporate, administrative, or remote access. HPE's) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 284.0 Td (two-factor \(2FA\) posture is phishing-resistant by design:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 264.0 Td (- Primary authenticator: FIDO2 / WebAuthn security keys, delivered as company-issued YubiKeys,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 250.0 Td (  are the required strong authenticator for privileged, administrative, and high-risk roles.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 236.0 Td (  Hardware keys bind authentication to physical possession and defeat credential-replay and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 222.0 Td (  adversary-in-the-middle attacks.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 208.0 Td (- Biometric verification: Platform authenticators \(Windows Hello for Business, Touch ID\) using) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 194.0 Td (  biometric factors are approved for workstation-bound WebAuthn flows.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 180.0 Td (- Fallback factors: Okta Verify push with number matching is permitted for standard users. SMS) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 166.0 Td (  and voice one-time passcodes are deprecated and disallowed for any privileged context.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 146.0 Td (Step-up MFA is enforced adaptively by Okta and Entra ID Conditional Access based on device posture,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 132.0 Td (network location, and risk signals.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 106.0 Td (4. Password and Passphrase Standards) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 83.0 Td (Where a password or passphrase is still required-for account recovery, non-federated systems, or the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 69.0 Td (primary identity store-the following standards apply:) Tj ET
endstream
