stream
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 738.0 Td (- Length: A minimum passphrase length of 14 characters for standard accounts and 16 characters) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 724.0 Td (  for privileged accounts. Length is prioritized over arbitrary complexity.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 710.0 Td (- Complexity: Passwords must not appear in known-breach corpora; HPE screens all new and changed) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 696.0 Td (  passwords against a compromised-credential dictionary. Composition rules encourage passphrases) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 682.0 Td (  over cryptic strings.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 668.0 Td (- Expiry: In alignment with NIST SP 800-63B guidance, time-based password expiry is eliminated) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 654.0 Td (  for accounts protected by phishing-resistant MFA. Credentials are rotated on evidence of) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 640.0 Td (  compromise rather than on a fixed calendar. Service account secrets retain a maximum 90-day) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 626.0 Td (  rotation.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 612.0 Td (- Password reuse across corporate and personal accounts is strictly prohibited, and account) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 598.0 Td (  lockout thresholds throttle brute-force attempts.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 572.0 Td (5. Credential, Secret, and Key Management) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 549.0 Td (All non-interactive credentials-including API tokens, secrets, signing keys, and X.509) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 535.0 Td (certificates-must be stored in an approved enterprise secrets vault \(HashiCorp Vault or the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 521.0 Td (cloud-native key management service\) and never embedded in source code, configuration files, or) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 507.0 Td (container images. Each credential MUST have a defined owner, a documented rotation interval, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 493.0 Td (automated expiry. TLS and code-signing certificates are managed through the corporate PKI with) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 479.0 Td (monitored lifecycles to prevent outages and mis-issuance. Cryptographic key material is generated,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 465.0 Td (stored, and retired in accordance with HPE's key management standard, using hardware security) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 451.0 Td (modules for root and intermediate keys. Automated scanning detects leaked secrets and tokens in) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 437.0 Td (repositories and pipelines, triggering immediate revocation.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 411.0 Td (6. Lifecycle, Governance, and Enforcement) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 388.0 Td (Identity lifecycle events-joiner, mover, leaver-are automated through Entra ID and Okta provisioning) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 374.0 Td (connectors driven by the authoritative HR system. Access is granted on least-privilege and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 360.0 Td (role-based principles, reviewed quarterly through access certification campaigns. Privileged) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 346.0 Td (accounts require just-in-time elevation and are subject to session recording. Violations of this) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 332.0 Td (policy may result in disciplinary action up to and including termination and, where applicable,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 318.0 Td (legal referral.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 292.0 Td (7. Review) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 269.0 Td (This policy is reviewed at least annually by the CISO organization and updated in response to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 255.0 Td (material changes in threat landscape, technology, or regulatory obligation.) Tj ET
endstream
